---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import InvestorLogo from '../../components/InvestorLogo.astro';
import { investors } from '../../data/investors';

const proceeds = [
  ['40%', 'Compute, including an additional 6,000 couches'],
  ['30%', 'Snacks'],
  ['20%', 'Talent, compensated in kibble'],
  ['10%', 'A larger bed'],
];
---

<Base
  title="Pugalarity Labs Announces $4.2 Quadrillion Series Z"
  description="Pugalarity Labs raises $4.2 quadrillion in Series Z funding at a valuation of one (1) very good boy."
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl">
    <header>
      <p class="text-accent font-mono text-sm uppercase tracking-wider">News · Press release</p>
      <h1 class="mt-2 text-4xl font-semibold leading-tight sm:text-5xl">
        Pugalarity Labs raises $4.2 quadrillion Series Z at a valuation of one (1) very good boy
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted mt-4 font-mono text-sm">
        <time datetime="2026-10-28">October 28, 2026</time> · Couch Valley
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <p>
        <strong>COUCH VALLEY</strong> — Pugalarity Labs, the safety-focused superintelligence
        company, today announced a $4.2 quadrillion Series Z financing round. The round values the
        company at one (1) very good boy.
      </p>
      <p>
        The financing was led by Kibble Capital and Lapdog Ventures, with participation from
        Sunbeam Sovereign Fund, Squeak &amp; Partners, and Late Brunch Partners. It brings the
        company’s total funding to more than every other number.
      </p>

      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “This round allows us to scale responsibly. Responsibly, in this context, means a lot of
          couches.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">
          Sir Reginald Wrinkles, Chief Executive Pug
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Use of proceeds</h2>
      <p>Pugalarity Labs intends to allocate the new capital as follows:</p>
    </div>

    <dl class="border-rule divide-rule mt-4 divide-y border-y text-lg">
      {
        proceeds.map(([pct, what]) => (
          <div class="grid grid-cols-[5rem_1fr] gap-4 py-3">
            <dt class="font-mono font-medium tabular-nums">{pct}</dt>
            <dd>{what}</dd>
          </div>
        ))
      }
    </dl>

    <div class="mt-8 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <blockquote class="border-accent border-l-4 pl-5">
        <p>
          “We have seen a lot of pitch decks. This is the first one that was also asleep for most
          of the meeting. That is the kind of conviction we back.”
        </p>
        <footer class="text-muted mt-2 text-base">
          Gus Fawnsworth, Managing Partner, Kibble Capital
        </footer>
      </blockquote>

      <h2 class="pt-4 text-2xl font-semibold">Our investors</h2>
    </div>
    <ul class="text-muted mt-4 flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-10 gap-y-6">
      {
        investors.map((i) => (
          <li>
            <InvestorLogo firm={i.firm} class="h-8 w-auto" />
          </li>
        ))
      }
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-10 space-y-5 text-lg leading-relaxed">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">About Pugalarity Labs</h2>
      <p>
        Pugalarity Labs is building safe, beneficial superintelligence that is also very good at
        sitting. The company’s flagship model, Snort-1, is available in private preview.{' '}
        <a href="/waitlist/" class="underline underline-offset-4">Join the waitlist.</a>
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Media contact</h2>
      <p>Please bark.</p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-semibold">Forward-looking statements</h2>
      <p class="text-muted text-base">
        This announcement contains forward-looking statements, including statements about future
        naps. Actual results may differ materially, particularly if someone opens a bag.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
